# NGINX 1.30.4 single-process mode allocates its event connection/read/write
# arrays in ngx_event_process_init and intentionally leaves them live until
# process exit. The sanitizer harness uses single-process mode so LeakSanitizer
# can observe the module in the serving process. Keep this suppression at the
# upstream allocation function so request, codec, and module leaks still fail.
leak:ngx_event_process_init
